# Sim and coordinates

World: +X east, +Y **south** (Ebiten Y-down). Lot **400×288**. Origin NW. Spawn `(200, 248)`, heading `0` = north.

```go
// heading 0 → north (0, -1); heading increases clockwise
func Forward(heading float64) (fx, fy float64) {
    return math.Sin(heading), -math.Cos(heading)
}
```

`A` = vehicle **left** (heading decreases). Reverse is first-class. Camera is world-fixed north and **does not yaw**.

Physics uses continuous `heading`. Facing index is draw-only.

## Solidity

Dozer body is a circle (`DozerBodyR`). Structure cells and rubble are AABBs. Resolve with `CircleAABB` (max 3 iterations). No physics engine.

Cells: Intact → Cracked → Broken (dust) → Rubble. Blade damages **only overlapped cells**. Roofs collapse when support drops (delayed hops). Rubble is real collision (sprite inset). **Never delete rubble.** Fragments/dust do not collide.

## Heat, plates, threats

Heat and plates are sprite state. One cruiser hunts after the first wreck. Frontal blade-down kills the cruiser; side/rear peel when blade is up.

Simulation order is `stepPlay` in `sim.go`. `R` resets the sandbox.
